{"skill":{"slug":"feishu-messaging","displayName":"Feishu Messaging"},"version":{"version":"0.0.3","createdAt":1770355651477,"changelog":"- 移除文档中“SDK 使用说明”相关注释，使示例代码部分更简洁。\n- 精简了部分代码注释，去除了冗余的“复制该 Demo 后...”说明。\n- 其余功能和结构保持不变。","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6656,"sha256":"8f32198df00ffb8d9996ef1dfeb8428207bbde528bd9dbe16be053c7802d17d9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2036,"sha256":"afaf0b1046390efc47b6072e42c2145439085ade077c71d758c88ff3985c3c6b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036368998,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"26c1a1aed4f7e42b17812f58ff63636b0fbc63be1d8a17a8279ae23f1fa1452e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/26c1a1aed4f7e42b17812f58ff63636b0fbc63be1d8a17a8279ae23f1fa1452e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: feishu-messaging\nVersion: 0.0.3\n\nThe OpenClaw skill bundle for Feishu messaging appears benign. It provides Python code examples for interacting with the Feishu API to send messages, upload images/files, and manage chat members using the `lark_oapi` SDK. While the skill demonstrates local file access for uploading images and videos, this is a legitimate function for a messaging skill and there is no evidence of intent to exfiltrate sensitive data or execute malicious commands. The SKILL.md instructions are descriptive and do not contain any prompt injection attempts with malicious objectives.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161784828},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":37,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789036368998},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is mostly a Feishu messaging helper, but it under-discloses file upload and organizational metadata handling while encouraging verbose logging of sensitive API responses.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of Feishu app credentials and Feishu API network access is proportionate for messaging, but examples use DEBUG logging and full response serialization, which can expose tenant metadata in terminals, transcripts, or logs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected package contains only a Markdown skill file and no executable installer, bundled script, dependency manifest, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions include Feishu chat search, member retrieval, message sending, image upload, and file upload; these are user-directed examples, but the skill does not clearly warn that local files, message content, chat IDs, and member data may be sent to or returned from Feishu.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, background worker, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, memory writes, or cross-session modification behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose covers Feishu messaging and mentions document creation, chat lookup, and member lookup, but the artifact provides no document-creation workflow and includes image/file upload examples that are not listed in the core capability table or permissions summary.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing or using in a tenant environment. Limit the Feishu app to the minimum permissions needed, avoid copying the DEBUG logging and full-response logging patterns, confirm recipients and file paths before sending, and treat chat/member lookup results and uploaded files as sensitive organizational data.","findings":"[SDI-1] unexpected: The scanner's mismatch concern is partially supported: document creation is claimed in the description but not implemented in the artifact, which is inaccurate but not independently malicious.\n[SDI-1] expected: Chat lookup and member lookup are disclosed in the trigger and capability table, but image/file upload is present only in later examples and is not reflected in the core capability or permission summary.\n[SQP-2] expected: Group and member lookup are purpose-aligned for finding Feishu recipients, but they access organizational metadata and the skill does not give least-privilege or privacy guidance.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending messages and uploading media to Feishu is expected for this kind of skill, but users should be clearly warned before transmitting sensitive message bodies or local files under organizational credentials.\n[SDI-2] expected: Image and file upload can fit a messaging workflow, but the artifact does not scope upload sources, file sensitivity, or required permissions clearly enough.\n[T09] unexpected: The static logging concern is supported by repeated examples that enable DEBUG logging and print complete successful and failed API response data without redaction.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036368998}}}}}